WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.060 --> 00:00:03.179
Yippee-ki-yay, movie lovers, it's Jan here.

00:00:03.179 --> 00:00:07.350
I've just seen X-Men: Apocalypse and can confirm
there's a single post-credits scene right

00:00:07.350 --> 00:00:09.320
at the very end of the movie's credits.

00:00:09.320 --> 00:00:13.440
In this video, I'm going to break down and
explain what's in the scene and what it means

00:00:13.440 --> 00:00:16.770
for future X-Men movies, so there will be
spoilers.

00:00:16.770 --> 00:00:21.230
If you want to avoid any spoilers, click here
for my spoiler-free review or come back after

00:00:21.230 --> 00:00:22.630
you've seen the movie.

00:00:22.630 --> 00:00:26.429
The post-credits scene begins with a small
group of men in black suits walking through

00:00:26.429 --> 00:00:30.900
the corridors of the Weapon X facility while
a clean-up operation is in progress.

00:00:30.900 --> 00:00:34.950
Blood and bodies are being cleared from the
floor and bullets are also being vacuumed

00:00:34.950 --> 00:00:35.950
up.

00:00:35.950 --> 00:00:39.860
One of the suited men who wears glasses also
carries a briefcase and he uses a key card

00:00:39.860 --> 00:00:44.400
to enter one of the labs where we see x-rays
of a body and skulls, reminiscent of the x-rays

00:00:44.400 --> 00:00:48.140
from the Alkali Lake facility that first appeared
in the second X-Men movie.

00:00:48.140 --> 00:00:52.870
In the lab, the suited man takes a vial of
dark red liquid labelled "Weapon X", which

00:00:52.870 --> 00:00:57.550
is likely a sample of Wolverine's blood, and
he puts it in his briefcase which has at least

00:00:57.550 --> 00:01:00.580
3 other vials in it each with different coloured
liquids.

00:01:00.580 --> 00:01:04.190
The colours in the other vials are green,
yellow and there's another with an almost

00:01:04.190 --> 00:01:05.379
clear liquid.

00:01:05.379 --> 00:01:10.240
As the man closes the briefcase, we see a
large chrome label with the words "Essex Corp".

00:01:10.240 --> 00:01:15.009
The name Essex is a huge tease for the comic
book villain Mr Sinister, also known as Dr

00:01:15.009 --> 00:01:16.240
Nathanial Essex.

00:01:16.240 --> 00:01:21.240
In the comics, Nathanial Essex is a Darwinist
geneticist obsessed with developing a superior

00:01:21.240 --> 00:01:22.240
species.

00:01:22.240 --> 00:01:26.159
He shares an outlook with Apocalypse that
only the strongest should survive and he actually

00:01:26.159 --> 00:01:30.100
works with him after Apocalypse turns him
into Mr Sinister, which is the last word his

00:01:30.100 --> 00:01:32.090
wife said to him on her death bed.

00:01:32.090 --> 00:01:36.789
In the comics, Sinister has a history of collecting
genetic material from mutants, and in the

00:01:36.789 --> 00:01:41.430
Weapon X comics he surreptitiously collected
a vial of blood from Marvel's first mutant

00:01:41.430 --> 00:01:44.979
Namor when he was injured by the Nazis during
World War 2.

00:01:44.979 --> 00:01:49.670
Sinister then used Namor's blood for his experiments,
creating a clone of Namor that he tried out

00:01:49.670 --> 00:01:50.780
against Captain America.

00:01:50.780 --> 00:01:56.209
So, if that is indeed Wolverine's blood in
the vial in X-Men: Apocalypse, that could

00:01:56.209 --> 00:02:01.930
be a big hint that we'll see the female Wolverine
clone X-23 appear in Wolverine 3.

00:02:01.930 --> 00:02:07.040
Producer Simon Kinberg has already pitched
a female Wolverine character to Fox and Hugh

00:02:07.040 --> 00:02:10.739
Jackman has said the next Wolverine solo movie
will be his last.

00:02:10.739 --> 00:02:15.489
Cloning X-23 from Wolverine's genetic material
could be an interesting way to introduce an

00:02:15.489 --> 00:02:19.080
alternate version of one of Fox's most popular
mutants to date.

00:02:19.080 --> 00:02:24.439
By the way, Deadpool director Tim Miller has
said he'd love to see Deadpool fight X-23.

00:02:24.439 --> 00:02:26.930
And what about those other vials in the briefcase?

00:02:26.930 --> 00:02:31.659
Well, Wolverine 3 casting has confirmed we're
getting Richard E. Grant as a "villainous

00:02:31.659 --> 00:02:36.480
mad-scientist type" so he could be the movie
version of Doctor Abraham Cornelius, a Weapon

00:02:36.480 --> 00:02:41.470
X scientist working on replicating Wolverine
and other mutants' powers in the comics.

00:02:41.470 --> 00:02:46.081
If Mr Sinister has been able to collect genetic
material from any of the other X-Men who were

00:02:46.081 --> 00:02:50.590
trapped at Stryker's Weapon X building, it's
always possible we'd see clones of them in

00:02:50.590 --> 00:02:52.069
future films.

00:02:52.069 --> 00:02:56.930
And if he has any of Jean Grey's genes he
could create her clone Madelyne Pryor, which

00:02:56.930 --> 00:02:58.409
he creates in the comics.

00:02:58.409 --> 00:03:03.040
Cable, who's the child of Cyclops and Madelyne
Prior, is confirmed as appearing in Deadpool

00:03:03.040 --> 00:03:07.329
2, so we could see Sinister involved in Cable's
origin story.

00:03:07.329 --> 00:03:11.549
Mr Sinister is a major villain in the X-Men
comics and Simon Kinberg has said that he

00:03:11.549 --> 00:03:14.810
could show up in the Gambit movie as well
as the X-Men films.

00:03:14.810 --> 00:03:19.469
In the comics, Remy LeBeau has a history of
working with Dr Essex as an agent of his,

00:03:19.469 --> 00:03:23.370
so assuming the Gambit solo movie does get
made, it looks likely Mr Sinister will pop

00:03:23.370 --> 00:03:24.370
up there.

00:03:24.370 --> 00:03:28.909
I think Mr Sinister could be used to build
up a more unified X-Men movie universe in

00:03:28.909 --> 00:03:33.420
a similar way to how Marvel Studios have used
Thanos to tie together its different superheroes

00:03:33.420 --> 00:03:36.140
and villains and build them towards Infinity
War.

00:03:36.140 --> 00:03:40.780
So guys, what did you think about the post-credits
tease for Mr Sinister and who would you like

00:03:40.780 --> 00:03:42.349
to see cast as the villain?

00:03:42.349 --> 00:03:46.379
Bryan Cranston already said he'd really like
to play Mr Sinister at New York Comic Con

00:03:46.379 --> 00:03:49.579
last year, so do you think he'd be a good
choice?

